~/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata/<APPID>/compatibilitytool.cfgExample script to set a specific Proton version for one game:
#!/bin/bash
APPID="123456"  # Replace with your game's AppID
PROTON_VERSION="proton_ge_9-12"  # Match the folder name exactly

echo "compat_tool_name=$PROTON_VERSION" > \
  "$HOME/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata/$APPID/compatibilitytool.cfg"
Batch update multiple games:
#!/bin/bash
PROTON="proton_8.0"

for app in "$HOME/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata"/*/; do
    APPID=$(basename "$app")
    echo "compat_tool_name=$PROTON" > "$app/compatibilitytool.cfg"
    echo "Set $APPID to $PROTON"
done
Method 2: Environment Variables at Launch
You can override the compatibility tool when launching a game:
# Set Proton version via environment variable
STEAM_COMPAT_TOOL_PATH="/path/to/Proton/version" \
STEAM_COMPAT_DATA_PATH="$HOME/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata/<APPID>" \
steam://run/<APPID>
Or use the Steam URL scheme with beta parameters:
steam://run/<APPID>//?beta=proton
Method 3: Using steamtinkerlaunch
This is a more robust tool for managing compatibility settings:
# Install steamtinkerlaunch
steamtinkerlaunch compat add

# Set compatibility tool for a specific game
steamtinkerlaunch compat set <APPID> proton_ge_9-12
Method 4: Using Protontricks
While protontricks is primarily for installing Windows dependencies, you can combine it with other methods:
# First set the compatibility tool, then use protontricks for dependencies
echo "compat_tool_name=proton_ge_9-12" > \
  "$HOME/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata/<APPID>/compatibilitytool.cfg"

protontricks <APPID> winetricks_command
Important Notes

Steam must be restarted after editing compatibilitytool.cfg for changes to take effect
Folder names matter - match the exact Proton folder name in ~/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatibilitytools.d/
Steam may overwrite settings - if you change settings through the GUI, it will overwrite your script's changes
For Flatpak Steam - paths may differ (check ~/.var/app/com.valvesoftware.Steam/)

Finding Your Game's AppID
You can find the AppID from:

Steam store page URL (e.g., store.steampowered.com/app/123456/)
Steam library (right-click → Properties)
Or list all compatdata folders:
ls ~/.steam/steam/steamapps/compatdata/


